WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.292
Lesson four point zero.

2
00:00:01.619 --> 00:00:04.124
Before any architecture: the rules every

3
00:00:04.124 --> 00:00:05.213
candidate must obey.

4
00:00:09.213 --> 00:00:10.986
Topic four compares three kinds of learned

5
00:00:10.986 --> 00:00:12.842
drummer: an LSTM, a state-space model

6
00:00:12.842 --> 00:00:14.161
called S4D, and a transformer.

7
00:00:14.409 --> 00:00:16.264
Before any of them was built, one document

8
00:00:16.264 --> 00:00:17.831
fixed what every candidate must do,

9
00:00:17.831 --> 00:00:19.810
learned or not: the drum-stage contract,

10
00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.294
settled on the twelfth of September.

11
00:00:21.542 --> 00:00:23.315
If two candidates solve slightly different

12
00:00:23.315 --> 00:00:25.129
problems, the results table means nothing.

13
00:00:25.376 --> 00:00:26.984
So the contract fixes the shape of the

14
00:00:26.984 --> 00:00:28.634
function, and the rules that keep the

15
00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:29.376
comparison honest.

16
00:00:31.005 --> 00:00:33.653
In the contract's symbols: y hat t, the

17
00:00:33.653 --> 00:00:36.188
nine drum probabilities at slot t, is some

18
00:00:36.188 --> 00:00:38.723
function, f, of the guitar features from

19
00:00:38.723 --> 00:00:41.033
the start of the song up to slot t minus

20
00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:43.512
h, the model's own outputs up to the slot

21
00:00:43.512 --> 00:00:45.935
before, and c, what is known about the

22
00:00:45.935 --> 00:00:46.217
song.

23
00:00:46.705 --> 00:00:49.012
So three things may feed slot t: the

24
00:00:49.012 --> 00:00:51.209
guitar heard so far, the drums it has

25
00:00:51.209 --> 00:00:53.680
already given, and what is known about the

26
00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:53.955
song.

27
00:00:54.285 --> 00:00:56.921
In the code there is no separate c: things

28
00:00:56.921 --> 00:00:59.173
like whether the song's velocity is real

29
00:00:59.173 --> 00:01:01.260
ride in with the five inputs at every

30
00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:01.535
slot.

31
00:01:01.991 --> 00:01:04.184
The horizon, h, is fixed at one: the drums

32
00:01:04.184 --> 00:01:05.870
for slot t are decided having heard the

33
00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.431
guitar only through slot t minus one.

34
00:01:07.684 --> 00:01:09.413
One slot lasts sixty over four times the

35
00:01:09.413 --> 00:01:10.256
tempo, in seconds.

36
00:01:10.509 --> 00:01:12.365
At a hundred and twenty beats per minute,

37
00:01:12.365 --> 00:01:13.757
that's a hundred and twenty-five

38
00:01:13.757 --> 00:01:14.811
milliseconds of headroom.

39
00:01:15.064 --> 00:01:16.456
At two hundred it's seventy-five.

40
00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.480
The budget is a slot, so it tightens as

41
00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:19.281
the song speeds up.

42
00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:21.137
And h must be the same in training as

43
00:01:21.137 --> 00:01:21.348
live.

44
00:01:21.808 --> 00:01:24.456
One small difference from the document: in

45
00:01:24.456 --> 00:01:26.938
the code, f hands out nine logits, and a

46
00:01:26.938 --> 00:01:29.144
sigmoid turns each into the probability

47
00:01:29.144 --> 00:01:30.247
the contract writes.

48
00:01:33.697 --> 00:01:35.037
Recap from lesson one point two.

49
00:01:35.288 --> 00:01:37.381
Every slot, five numbers go in: the guitar

50
00:01:37.381 --> 00:01:38.930
onset, its velocity, the running

51
00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:40.773
intensity, a flag for whether this song's

52
00:01:40.773 --> 00:01:42.489
velocity is real at all, and the tempo.

53
00:01:42.741 --> 00:01:44.457
The onset, velocity and intensity come

54
00:01:44.457 --> 00:01:46.341
from the slot before: the loader shifts

55
00:01:46.341 --> 00:01:48.142
the guitar one slot later before any model

56
00:01:48.142 --> 00:01:49.859
sees it, so the future is never handed

57
00:01:49.859 --> 00:01:50.068
over.

58
00:01:50.319 --> 00:01:51.868
Nine logits come out, one per drum.

59
00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:53.794
Each is its own yes or no, so several

60
00:01:53.794 --> 00:01:54.715
drums can hit at once.

61
00:01:55.061 --> 00:01:57.915
In the code, B songs of C slots go in as B

62
00:01:57.915 --> 00:02:00.579
by C by five, and come out as B by C by

63
00:02:00.579 --> 00:02:00.896
nine.

64
00:02:01.277 --> 00:02:04.004
How hard each drum hits, and how far off

65
00:02:04.004 --> 00:02:06.351
the grid, are not this stage's job.

66
00:02:09.923 --> 00:02:12.471
Three rules from lesson three point four,

67
00:02:12.471 --> 00:02:13.745
now as the contract's.

68
00:02:14.093 --> 00:02:16.525
Causal: slot t uses nothing after it.

69
00:02:16.872 --> 00:02:19.015
Live there is no future to use, so

70
00:02:19.015 --> 00:02:20.926
training must not use one either.

71
00:02:21.915 --> 00:02:24.185
Second: the state runs through the whole

72
00:02:24.185 --> 00:02:24.432
song.

73
00:02:24.728 --> 00:02:26.702
It's carried from chunk to chunk, and

74
00:02:26.702 --> 00:02:28.331
never reset at a window boundary.

75
00:02:28.627 --> 00:02:30.453
It starts fresh only when a new song

76
00:02:30.453 --> 00:02:30.799
starts.

77
00:02:31.245 --> 00:02:33.403
Third: at each chunk edge the state is

78
00:02:33.403 --> 00:02:33.845
detached.

79
00:02:34.139 --> 00:02:36.445
The memory crosses the edge; the learning

80
00:02:36.445 --> 00:02:37.230
signal does not.

81
00:02:40.673 --> 00:02:42.208
So every model offers the same three

82
00:02:42.208 --> 00:02:44.032
calls, written at the top of model dot py.

83
00:02:44.281 --> 00:02:45.194
This is the interface.

84
00:02:45.442 --> 00:02:47.392
init state: a fresh memory for a batch of

85
00:02:47.392 --> 00:02:47.640
songs.

86
00:02:47.889 --> 00:02:49.880
The forward call: a chunk of slots and the

87
00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:51.870
state go in; logits and the new state come

88
00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:52.036
out.

89
00:02:52.285 --> 00:02:54.234
The third argument, prev out, is the drums

90
00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:55.022
of the slot before.

91
00:02:55.271 --> 00:02:56.681
Every model we compare ignores it.

92
00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.879
detach state: keep the numbers, cut the

93
00:02:58.879 --> 00:03:00.165
gradient, at each chunk edge.

94
00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.490
What the state is differs completely.

95
00:03:02.811 --> 00:03:05.375
The LSTM's is two small vectors per layer:

96
00:03:05.375 --> 00:03:07.566
five hundred and twelve numbers per song.

97
00:03:07.886 --> 00:03:10.184
S4D's is one tensor of complex numbers per

98
00:03:10.184 --> 00:03:12.535
layer, sixteen thousand three hundred and

99
00:03:12.535 --> 00:03:15.153
eighty-four of them: thirty-two thousand,

100
00:03:15.153 --> 00:03:17.023
seven hundred and sixty-eight real

101
00:03:17.023 --> 00:03:17.450
numbers.

102
00:03:17.771 --> 00:03:20.282
The transformer's is its key-value cache:

103
00:03:20.282 --> 00:03:22.419
what it computed for up to two thousand

104
00:03:22.419 --> 00:03:24.770
and forty-seven earlier slots, kept so it

105
00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.441
can look back at them, and a slot counter:

106
00:03:27.441 --> 00:03:29.471
seven hundred and eighty-six thousand

107
00:03:29.471 --> 00:03:30.433
numbers when full.

108
00:03:30.754 --> 00:03:32.410
The trainer never looks inside.

109
00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.013
It hands the state back.

110
00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.829
The trainer calls exactly these: a fresh

111
00:03:37.829 --> 00:03:39.844
state at a song's first chunk, the forward

112
00:03:39.844 --> 00:03:41.545
call, and a detach after every step.

113
00:03:41.813 --> 00:03:43.649
The live loop calls the same ones, one

114
00:03:43.649 --> 00:03:45.036
slot at a time, for one song.

115
00:03:45.305 --> 00:03:46.827
Neither one names an architecture.

116
00:03:47.096 --> 00:03:49.065
That's what let the transformer, added on

117
00:03:49.065 --> 00:03:51.169
the twenty-sixth of September, drop in:

118
00:03:51.169 --> 00:03:53.005
its cache is carried and detached by the

119
00:03:53.005 --> 00:03:54.571
trainer just like the LSTM's state.

120
00:03:57.957 --> 00:04:00.123
The contract also settled what a candidate

121
00:04:00.123 --> 00:04:00.777
may remember.

122
00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.843
Two things sound alike and are not.

123
00:04:03.145 --> 00:04:05.009
Memory: a state over the guitar.

124
00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.023
The model remembers what it heard.

125
00:04:07.326 --> 00:04:09.542
Output feedback: the drums it actually

126
00:04:09.542 --> 00:04:11.758
played at the slot before, fed back in as

127
00:04:11.758 --> 00:04:12.060
input.

128
00:04:12.363 --> 00:04:13.974
The model remembers what it did.

129
00:04:14.447 --> 00:04:16.963
Option A: a fixed stretch of guitar in,

130
00:04:16.963 --> 00:04:18.140
drums out, no state.

131
00:04:18.461 --> 00:04:20.762
The same local guitar always gets the same

132
00:04:20.762 --> 00:04:21.083
drums.

133
00:04:21.404 --> 00:04:22.903
The contract calls that the

134
00:04:22.903 --> 00:04:25.151
density-follower's ceiling, and says it

135
00:04:25.151 --> 00:04:25.739
cannot win.

136
00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:28.415
Option B: a memory of the guitar, no

137
00:04:28.415 --> 00:04:28.897
feedback.

138
00:04:29.218 --> 00:04:31.679
Same guitar, different history, different

139
00:04:31.679 --> 00:04:32.001
drums.

140
00:04:32.322 --> 00:04:34.623
Option C: B, plus the drums it just

141
00:04:34.623 --> 00:04:35.800
played, fed back in.

142
00:04:36.121 --> 00:04:38.208
It can stay in step with what actually

143
00:04:38.208 --> 00:04:40.777
sounded, at a risk called exposure bias:

144
00:04:40.777 --> 00:04:43.185
it trains on the real drummer's past, then

145
00:04:43.185 --> 00:04:44.416
has to play on its own.

146
00:04:44.925 --> 00:04:47.045
The decision: B is the default.

147
00:04:47.399 --> 00:04:49.754
In B the state already carries what the

148
00:04:49.754 --> 00:04:51.168
model was about to play.

149
00:04:51.521 --> 00:04:54.171
The LSTM, S4D and T128 are all option B,

150
00:04:54.171 --> 00:04:56.762
the transformer included: its cache is

151
00:04:56.762 --> 00:04:59.353
built from what it heard, never from what

152
00:04:59.353 --> 00:04:59.942
it played.

153
00:05:00.446 --> 00:05:03.170
C is a flag, not a rewrite: built on the

154
00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:05.554
sixteenth of October, it joins the nine

155
00:05:05.554 --> 00:05:07.654
drums of the slot before to the five

156
00:05:07.654 --> 00:05:09.584
guitar numbers, fourteen inputs.

157
00:05:09.925 --> 00:05:12.365
The one option C drummer trained so far is

158
00:05:12.365 --> 00:05:14.125
silent when it runs on its own.

159
00:05:14.465 --> 00:05:16.565
Lesson four point eight is about why.

160
00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.088
A fair comparison also needs the same food

161
00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:23.064
and the same cooking.

162
00:05:23.343 --> 00:05:25.294
Every arm of the architecture run got one

163
00:05:25.294 --> 00:05:27.339
shared list of settings: the same Lakh

164
00:05:27.339 --> 00:05:29.291
songs, the same four hundred validation

165
00:05:29.291 --> 00:05:31.010
songs, twelve epochs, batches of

166
00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.101
thirty-two, Adam at a learning rate of one

167
00:05:33.101 --> 00:05:35.053
in a thousand after three hundred warm-up

168
00:05:35.053 --> 00:05:37.144
steps, unweighted cross-entropy, dropout

169
00:05:37.144 --> 00:05:39.281
of a tenth, clipping at one, and one seed.

170
00:05:39.748 --> 00:05:41.490
And it shows in the run records.

171
00:05:41.817 --> 00:05:44.103
The LSTM, S4D and transformer runs each

172
00:05:44.103 --> 00:05:46.226
used fourteen thousand two hundred and

173
00:05:46.226 --> 00:05:48.621
fifty-six songs, two thousand one hundred

174
00:05:48.621 --> 00:05:50.853
and five steps in the first epoch, the

175
00:05:50.853 --> 00:05:53.357
same slots, and the same validation list,

176
00:05:53.357 --> 00:05:55.807
with the same seed and plan: their step

177
00:05:55.807 --> 00:05:57.331
counts match epoch by epoch.

178
00:05:59.096 --> 00:06:00.475
Three honest exceptions.

179
00:06:00.819 --> 00:06:03.289
One S4D run, S128 full, trained on all

180
00:06:03.289 --> 00:06:05.357
forty-seven thousand training songs.

181
00:06:05.702 --> 00:06:08.459
How far the gradient reaches differs: five

182
00:06:08.459 --> 00:06:10.354
hundred and twelve slots for the

183
00:06:10.354 --> 00:06:12.767
short-horizon LSTM and S4D, and for the

184
00:06:12.767 --> 00:06:15.294
transformer, two thousand and forty-eight

185
00:06:15.294 --> 00:06:16.787
for the long-horizon ones.

186
00:06:17.132 --> 00:06:19.544
The transformer's attention still reaches

187
00:06:19.544 --> 00:06:21.210
two thousand and forty-eight.

188
00:06:21.555 --> 00:06:24.025
And the transformer is told where it is in

189
00:06:24.025 --> 00:06:26.092
the bar, by a sixteen-entry table.

190
00:06:26.437 --> 00:06:28.907
The recurrent models have to count it from

191
00:06:28.907 --> 00:06:29.481
slot zero.

192
00:06:33.347 --> 00:06:34.508
The last rule is size.

193
00:06:34.825 --> 00:06:37.254
A parameter, from lesson three point one,

194
00:06:37.254 --> 00:06:38.416
is any learned number.

195
00:06:38.733 --> 00:06:40.739
The parameter budget is how many each

196
00:06:40.739 --> 00:06:41.531
model may have.

197
00:06:41.848 --> 00:06:44.171
The plan said about two hundred thousand,

198
00:06:44.171 --> 00:06:45.650
give or take twenty percent.

199
00:06:46.083 --> 00:06:48.472
The LSTM has two hundred and two thousand,

200
00:06:48.472 --> 00:06:50.170
three hundred and seventy-seven.

201
00:06:50.489 --> 00:06:52.825
S4D has two hundred and one thousand, six

202
00:06:52.825 --> 00:06:55.001
hundred and nine: seven hundred and

203
00:06:55.001 --> 00:06:57.231
sixty-eight fewer, under half a percent.

204
00:06:57.549 --> 00:06:59.461
The transformer has two hundred and

205
00:06:59.461 --> 00:07:01.637
twenty-six thousand, eight hundred and

206
00:07:01.637 --> 00:07:02.274
fifty-seven.

207
00:07:02.723 --> 00:07:04.902
That's twelve percent more than the LSTM.

208
00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:07.718
Inside the plan's band, but not equal, and

209
00:07:07.718 --> 00:07:09.950
the report must say so: it's finding

210
00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:10.322
thirty.

211
00:07:10.641 --> 00:07:12.926
A transformer sized to match, sixty-four

212
00:07:12.926 --> 00:07:15.318
wide and four layers deep, two hundred and

213
00:07:15.318 --> 00:07:17.550
two thousand and fifty-seven, exists on

214
00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:17.869
paper.

215
00:07:18.188 --> 00:07:19.304
It was never trained.

216
00:07:20.828 --> 00:07:23.004
And equal weights would not mean equal

217
00:07:23.004 --> 00:07:23.282
cost.

218
00:07:23.617 --> 00:07:25.960
The memory each one carries differs about

219
00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:28.414
fifteen hundred fold: five hundred and

220
00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:30.702
twelve numbers against seven hundred and

221
00:07:30.702 --> 00:07:31.817
eighty-six thousand.

222
00:07:32.152 --> 00:07:34.439
One warm step, measured offline on one

223
00:07:34.439 --> 00:07:36.782
processor thread, takes zero point zero

224
00:07:36.782 --> 00:07:39.181
four one milliseconds for the LSTM, zero

225
00:07:39.181 --> 00:07:41.468
point one four three for S4D, and zero

226
00:07:41.468 --> 00:07:43.755
point two seven nine for the transformer.

227
00:07:44.089 --> 00:07:45.038
All far inside a

228
00:07:45.038 --> 00:07:47.492
hundred-and-twenty-five-millisecond slot,

229
00:07:47.492 --> 00:07:49.445
and inside lesson one point four's

230
00:07:49.445 --> 00:07:51.564
decision window of thirty-seven and a

231
00:07:51.564 --> 00:07:51.843
half.

232
00:07:53.531 --> 00:07:56.016
Say it in one breath: every drummer reads

233
00:07:56.016 --> 00:07:58.236
five numbers a slot and answers with nine

234
00:07:58.236 --> 00:08:00.879
logits, never from the future; carries its

235
00:08:00.879 --> 00:08:03.100
state through the song and detaches it at

236
00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.426
each chunk edge; offers the same three

237
00:08:05.426 --> 00:08:07.805
calls; remembers the guitar but not its

238
00:08:07.805 --> 00:08:10.184
own drums; and trains on the same songs

239
00:08:10.184 --> 00:08:12.564
the same way, at near, not equal, size.

240
00:08:12.881 --> 00:08:14.943
This pairs with the contract itself,

241
00:08:14.943 --> 00:08:17.322
sections one to five, and the model dot py

242
00:08:17.322 --> 00:08:19.595
row of Reading the code in part two of the

243
00:08:19.595 --> 00:08:20.494
course explainer.

244
00:08:20.811 --> 00:08:23.243
Next, lesson four point one: recurrent

245
00:08:23.243 --> 00:08:24.723
nets, and why they forget.

